From: Cargt <tim.carney@cargt.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/panel: ili9881c: run GLT0557201280IS1 at 60 Hz

The GLT0557201280IS1 mode used a 50 MHz pixel clock. With its 870 x 1312
total timing that is 43.8 Hz, which caps every animation on the 5.5"
panel at about 44 fps.

Raise the clock to 68.486 MHz (870 x 1312 x 60), keeping the burst-mode
DSI video and the wider vertical back porch the STM32MP25 needs for a
stable image. Over the 4 DSI lanes at RGB888 that is about 411 Mbit/s per
lane.

Tested on an STM32MP257F 00395-01/00365: the mode reads 60 Hz, the image
is stable, and a WebKit kiosk page went from 43 fps to about 56 fps.
---
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-ilitek-ili9881c.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-ilitek-ili9881c.c
@@ -1217,7 +1217,8 @@
 };
 
  static const struct drm_display_mode glt0557201280is1_default_mode = {
-	 .clock		= 50000,
+	 /* 870 x 1312 total at 60 Hz (was 50000: 43.8 Hz) */
+	 .clock		= 68486,
  
 	 .hdisplay	= 720,
 	 .hsync_start	= 720 + 60,
